 "definition": "Headline rule and control support (review R5; main.tex Sect. 4.2 'Headline rule', supplement Table S1 D11).\n\nRule (fixed by the PI before the final estimates): the pooled imputation ATT on electricity (health centres + daycares) is\nthe headline only if EACH use type has >= 10 control-pool buildings observed in >= 80% of the calendar months of the\ntreated post-period; otherwise the health-centre estimate is the headline and the pooled one is secondary.\n\nOperational definition used here (sample = the primary imputation frame of s04_analysis, electricity):\n  treated post-period calendar months of use u = the set of calendar months (yyyymm) in which >= 1 treated building of use u\n      in the analysis sample has an observed post month (e+1 .. e+12);\n  a control-pool building (2024-25 or 2023 selection, same use) is 'observed' in a month if that month is in the fit sample\n      (kWh > 0, before its own start minus the 3 trimmed months);\n  coverage of a building = observed months among the treated post-period months of its use / number of those months.\nThe json also gives the count under two variants (pooled treated post-period months of both uses; control months counted\nwithout the 3-month trim) so that the sensitivity of the rule's outcome to these readings is visible. The rule itself is not\nchanged here.\n\nSecond output: number of control-pool buildings observed per calendar month by use (and by selection group), next to the\nnumber of treated buildings with a post month in that calendar month -> supplement figure.\n\nNo network. Outputs: results/a_support_rule.json, results/a_support_controls_by_month.csv. Partial-data runs: debugging only.",
